Explanation of what changed:

1. We keep the existing `isLabelExternal` check (so you only add labels where you want them).
2. We pull out the label text via `getLabel(element)` as before.
3. If there is _no_ flow‐name but the flow carries a `messageRef`, we grab `messageRef.name` and even write it back to `semantic.name` so that the downstream label‐renderer will pick it up.
4. Only if we end up with a non‐empty `labelText` do we call `this.addLabel(…)`.

This will cause message‐flows whose BPMN `<messageFlow>` carries a `<message>` to render the name of that message on the diagram.
